  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cons. of strategic properties for neotrop. birds on the Appalachian Corridor II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will acquire 1,150 acres in fee simple or in conservation servitudes. Located in the Quebec Northern Green Mountains natural transborder corridor, these properties are strategically located in an 11,900-acre core area of unfragmented forest. They are also a crucial link in allowing the connectivity between the properties that are already protected. This project will also support and build capacity for the grantees 11 affiliate members. Among the species that will benefit Canada Warbler, Wood Thrush, Yellow-bellied Sapsucker and Scarlet Tanager.</narrative>
  </description>
